VERDICT: FAIL
CHECKER: checker-second
FAMILY: adversarial
TASK: R5
ATTEMPT: 1
---
Claim under attack: "get_balance_projection now honours as_of correctly for
historical and future dates, and the default (no as_of) path is unchanged."

Criteria 1 and 2 (historical/future as_of) hold up: read
internal/services/mcpsvc/ledger/accounts.go (registerGetBalanceProjection,
recurringForProjection) and internal/services/insights/recurring.go
(DetectRecurringAt, ReferenceDate, TransactionSetForRecurring). The existing
tests TestGetBalanceProjectionHistoricalAsOfSchedulesFromPastEvidenceOnly and
TestGetBalanceProjectionFutureAsOfEvaluatesFreshnessAgainstRequestedDate
exercise real divergences (verified by reading fixtures and re-running
`go test ./internal/services/mcpsvc/ledger/... -run TestGetBalanceProjection -v`,
both pass and the crossing/emptiness assertions are non-trivial).

Criterion 3 (default path unchanged) is FALSE. The worker's own pinned test,
TestGetBalanceProjectionDefaultAsOfUnchanged, explicitly uses a fixture with
"NO merchant with 3+ occurrences" (see its doc comment), so
insights.DetectRecurring/DetectRecurringAt both return nil regardless of
which reference date is used. It proves nothing about the actual code path
that changed.

`git diff 6bc508d -- internal/services/mcpsvc/ledger/accounts.go` shows the
real change on the default path: pre-R5, get_balance_projection passed the
UNTRUNCATED ts.Transactions into accounts.Project and called
recurringForProjection(deps, txns) -> insights.DetectRecurring(ts) i.e.
DetectRecurringAt(ts, zero) -> referenceDate falls back to ts.MaxDate().
Post-R5 (current tree), for the SAME no-as_of call, asOf := time.Now()
(unchanged line) is now (a) used to truncate the active set via
active.FilterByDateRange(active.MinDate(), asOf), and (b) threaded into
insights.DetectRecurringAt(ts, asOf) as referenceDate. Neither of these was
true before R5. time.Now() and ts.MaxDate() are different dates whenever the
ledger's last transaction isn't dated today -- the normal case for an
imported ledger.

Built two adversarial fixtures directly against the actual (uncommitted)
tree and reran with `go test -count=1 -v`, then reconstructed the exact
pre-R5 formula (`accounts.Project(acct, ts.Transactions, time.Now(), ...)`,
`insights.DetectRecurring(active)`) as a counterfactual and ran it against
the identical fixture for a direct comparison:

1. Recurring-detection count divergence (isolates R5's own diff): a ledger
   with three monthly $900 "Rent Payment" rows (2026-01-01..2026-03-01, real
   wall clock in this environment is 2026-08-19) gives
   insights.DetectRecurring(active) == 1 item (fresh, referenceDate =
   ts.MaxDate() = 2026-03-01, 0 days stale) but
   recurringForProjection(active, time.Now()) == 0 items (same series judged
   ~171 days stale against today, outside the 90-day monthly freshness
   window). Confirmed reproducibly with TZ=UTC and default TZ.

2. Decisive, non-masked output divergence (ReferenceAmount/HasReference,
   which reads txns directly with no time.Time map involved, so it isn't
   confounded by an unrelated pre-existing map-key bug in accounts.Project
   -- see note below): a two-account fixture (checking, brokerage) with one
   future-dated (2027-01-05, well after the real 2026-08-19 clock) paired
   internal transfer of $777 between them. Confirmed via deps.load() that
   the transfer classifies TransferClass=="paired" as expected. Calling the
   actual current-tree get_balance_projection with NO as_of on the brokerage
   account returns has_reference=false, reference_amount=0.00. Reconstructing
   the exact pre-R5 handler formula (accounts.Project(acct, ts.Transactions,
   time.Now(), nil) -- untruncated txns, matching what the code did before
   R5's diff) against the identical fixture returns has_reference=true,
   reference_amount=777.00. This is the same tool, the same account, the
   same data, the same "no as_of supplied" call, and the current tree
   answers "no reference amount" where the pre-R5 tree answered "$777" --
   directly contradicting "the default (no as_of) path is unchanged."

This happens because R5's truncation (`active.FilterByDateRange(all.MinDate(),
asOf)`, asOf=time.Now() on the default path) now excludes any transaction
dated after today, including future-dated/post-dated rows that pre-R5's
raw `ts.Transactions` included unfiltered. The R5 brief's acceptance
criterion 3 demanded the default path be pinned unchanged; it silently
changed for any ledger containing a future-dated transaction (post-dated
transfers, scheduled items, clock skew on import) -- and separately, for
the ordinary case of an imported ledger whose last row isn't dated today,
it changes which recurring merchants are judged "fresh" for the default
projection, per (1) above.

Supporting finding, not load-bearing for this verdict (pre-existing,
predates R5, and touches R3's territory which is out of scope/accepted):
dashboard's default projection asOf is the ledger's own MaxDate
(internal/handlers/dashboard/handlers.go line 110: "asOf := maxDate; if
asOf.IsZero() { asOf = time.Now() }"), while the MCP tool's default asOf is
time.Now() (accounts.go line 211, unchanged by R5). Built a fixture and
confirmed the two surfaces give different crossing dates/minimums for the
same account with no as_of on either side (dashboard: "Drops below $500
around Mar 2, 2026"; MCP default: crossing "2026-08-20", minimum 400.00).
TestDashboardAndMCPProjectionAgree (R3) only passes because it drives the
MCP side with an explicit as_of chosen to match the dashboard's implicit
maxDate default -- it does not, and cannot, cover the actual no-as_of/
no-as_of comparison. This is exactly the fixture-coincidence risk the
dispatch brief called out; it means "parity" is not structural for the
default path even after R5.

Separately noted, not pursued further (masks but does not resolve the
above): accounts.Project's byDay map is keyed by time.Time values built two
different ways -- occurrence dates derived from time.Parse-sourced dates
(time.UTC, the built-in singleton Location) vs asOfDay derived from
dayOf(time.Now()) (time.Local, a distinct *Location object even when
TZ=UTC is exported, confirmed: `time.Local == time.UTC` is false in this
environment both with and without TZ=UTC). Since Go's time.Time == uses
pointer-identity on Location, this silently drops ALL recurring-occurrence
byDay entries whenever asOf comes from time.Now() rather than a UTC-parsed
date -- i.e., on every default (no as_of) call, recurring items can never
move Crossing/Minimum/SuggestedTopUp regardless of whether detection
included them, which is why fixture #1 above needed the ReferenceAmount
field to get a clean signal. This bug predates R5 (projection.go is
untouched by R5's diff) and is out of R5's stated scope, but it materially
undermines any claim that the default path's Crossing/Minimum fields are
being meaningfully exercised by ANY existing test, worker's or otherwise.

Reran regressions after removing all temporary adversarial/debug files
(confirmed via diff against a pre-edit backup that internal/services/
accounts/projection.go is byte-identical to its state before this
investigation, and `git status` shows no zz_* leftovers):
- `go build ./...`: clean.
- `go vet ./...`: clean.
- `go test -race ./...`: all packages pass (dashboard_parity_test.go did not
  flake in this run).
- `go test ./internal/services/mcpsvc/ledger/... -v`: all tests pass,
  including R1/R3/R7-adjacent tests in the same package
  (TestGetTransfers*, TestResolveTransfer*, TestDashboardAndMCPProjectionAgree).

No regression was found in R1/R3/R7's own accepted behavior; the failure is
specific to R5's criterion 3.

